            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0710" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/2455: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-05T17:00:00-05:00">March 5, 1940—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Your 49, February 23, 10 p.m. The Colombian Ambassador here informed us that
                    he is awaiting the detailed information regarding specific projects essential to
                    the proper presentation of Colombia’s request for credits from the Export-Import
                    Bank. It is believed that the various agencies here concerned with the extension
                    of credits would prefer to have an exact idea of what Colombia desires to
                    achieve before offering comment as to the best ways of attaining these
                    objectives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
